q('A patient remains in septic shock despite apparently active antibiotics. Which response is most useful?', 'Reassess source control, susceptibility, exposure/dosing and alternative or mixed shock mechanisms',[
 ('Add antimicrobials indefinitely without reassessing the source','This can miss an undrained focus or a noninfectious driver.'),('Assume every persistent fever represents resistance','Inflammation and complications can persist for other reasons.'),('Stop hemodynamic assessment because the antibiotic matches the culture','Effective antimicrobial therapy does not immediately normalize circulation.')],
 'Persistent shock is a prompt to reassess the whole causal pathway', '**An uncontrolled source or inadequate drug exposure can sustain infection.**',['Confirm delivery, dosing and relevant tissue penetration.','Evaluate cardiac dysfunction, hemorrhage or obstruction when the picture suggests mixed shock.'], '**Use targeted investigations and intervention rather than indiscriminate escalation.**',['Repeat cultures and imaging when indicated.','Involve relevant critical-care, infectious-disease and procedural teams.'],[['Infection','Source and susceptibility'],['Drug','Dose, delivery and exposure'],['Circulation','Mixed or alternative shock']],[SS],style='clinical_scenario')

